1
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,817
Episode 1 Go get him, Zoro!

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,057
What are you waiting for?

3
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:13,970
Punch him out!

4
00:00:14,053 --> 00:00:15,077
Knock him on the floor!

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,837
You can't - I don't need a cheering squad!

6
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:17,979
Go hide somewhere!

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,497
All right, you guys.

8
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:22,756
Do you think you could make
this a little challenging?

9
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:29,560
Come on, Saru!

10
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,157
This is why we keep you around!

11
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,711
It's the only thing you can do, Al, right?

12
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:43,600
Hurry up and finish off those
ugly-looking, really bad, evil people!

13
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,457
What do you think you're doing?

14
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:47,370
Hold up!

15
00:00:47,453 --> 00:00:52,160
Primary rule to assassination says all
weaker targets are to be eliminated first.

16
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:56,127
We'll show you how professionals
handle these sorts of things.

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:58,440
What, you mean me?

18
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:01,020
Hold on just a minute.

19
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:03,937
Getting rid of me won't
accomplish anything at all.

20
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:06,777
Sure, I'm pretty and I know
how to dress, but that's it.

21
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:08,817
I really don't have any fighting skills.

22
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,100
Yes, we know.

23
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:11,456
It's fairly obvious.

24
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,576
As we said, picking off the weak ones
first is the fastest way to work.

25
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:26,980
Ah, and that's exactly why I told
her to shut up and hide somewhere.

26
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:43,540
Destiny, fate, dreams.

27
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:48,360
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

28
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:52,177
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

29
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:54,907
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

30
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:19,077
It's hard to look away, even
though it's blinding me.

31
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:22,857
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

32
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:25,997
I'm really, really stuck on you, oh, oh!

33
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:29,737
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

34
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,797
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

35
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:36,097
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

36
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:38,200
Believe in wonder.

37
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:48,317
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

38
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,377
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

39
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,777
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

40
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:57,117
Live how we want to.

41
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:00,757
There is no limit to us,
we have the power of love.

42
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,837
We don't wanna live ordinary life.

43
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,857
We have a chance to live in paradise.

44
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,900
We live in one another.

45
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:24,080
Luffy dead? Impossible!

46
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:25,780
I don't believe you!

47
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,740
Nonetheless, it's true.

48
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:33,740
Poor Straw Hat, buried
in the sands of Rainbase.

49
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:35,300
Dear Miss Wednesday.

50
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,217
If only he hadn't gotten
involved with you?

51
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,760
He might have lived a long and happy life.

52
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,680
You're a liar!

53
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,531
He couldn't be killed by the likes of you!

54
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:53,357
You know, it's only
because of his sacrifice.

55
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:56,157
That you're still alive to
Raven Rant at this moment!

56
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:58,717
You owe him your deepest thanks.

57
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:01,897
That way, maybe he'll
at least be able to...

58
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:03,440
Tell me where he is!

59
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:06,320
Did you come here just to torture me?

60
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,300
Be able to rest in peace.

61
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:16,277
That brainless little fool, when did
she manage to lose herself this time?

62
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:19,580
This is why I told her to
pipe down and hide. But no,

63
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:23,197
she has to go running off on her own
and make me waste time looking for her,

64
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:24,110
stupid Nami.

65
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,217
That's it, I can't run anymore.

66
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,020
I'll have to fight!

67
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:41,800
Like hell!

68
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,420
This is taking too long.

69
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,280
So hasty.

70
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,480
Zoro!

71
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:56,930
Zoro!

72
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:03,512
That stone column just split into pieces.

73
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,360
It didn't split.

74
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,900
It was sliced.

75
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:12,778
Only a swordsman could have
done something like that.

76
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:15,540
That's right.

77
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,280
You cut it, didn't you?

78
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,820
With those arms, huh?

79
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:28,960
You've got a rather
unusual body, don't you?

80
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:30,980
You noticed.

81
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:34,712
I ate the dice-dice fruit
making blades of my entire body.

82
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:36,600
You're him.

83
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:40,920
The swordsman who supposedly cut
down a hundred men at Whiskey Peak.

84
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:43,657
He's also the pirate who
turned down an invitation

85
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:46,477
to join Baroque work several
years ago at East Blue.

86
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,800
And cut down on Mr. Seven at the time.

87
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,940
That was you too?

88
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:53,010
You?

89
00:05:53,093 --> 00:05:54,217
That's a story that takes me back.

90
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,417
That little misunderstanding was your Mr.

91
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:59,794
Seven's fault for not accepting
the terms I offered him.

92
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:03,777
As I remember it, I made a
very generous proposition.

93
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:07,213
I said, sure, I'll join as
long as you make me your boss.

94
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,297
You're quite a comedian, aren't you?

95
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:13,797
Instead of meeting my terms, he
rather rudely took a slash at me,

96
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,998
so naturally I put him in his place.

97
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:21,920
Now, would you like to invite me to because
right now you guys look so ridiculous.

98
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,965
I wouldn't even accept the job

99
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:30,840
You think you can make a fool out of me?

100
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:37,100
You some swordsman from
an upstart pirate crew?

101
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,777
Maybe I am but what do
you think you guys are?

102
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:45,177
Puppets with no will of your own being
manipulated by crocodile into building his

103
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:47,917
fake utopia or maybe you're all just

104
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,917
little tin soldiers
all shine and no steel?

105
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:59,577
Miss double finger I know I know
you want to eliminate him don't you?

106
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:03,960
You do as you please I'll
take care of the girl.

107
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:06,020
Oh, Nami, be careful.

108
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:07,620
Okay, she's gone.

109
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,680
I guess her plan must have failed.

110
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:33,057
She wasn't able to stop the
rebel army at the entrance.

111
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,846
I wonder if Vivi and the
others are all right.

112
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:40,716
They're all fighting, putting
their lives on the line.

113
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,160
And here I am, running and hiding.

114
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:51,960
You heard me!

115
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,120
I need help!

116
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,242
I want you to build me a weapon!

117
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:56,980
Build you a weapon?

118
00:07:57,460 --> 00:08:00,401
And what are you gonna do
with it, hide behind it?

119
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,330
Dash.

120
00:08:01,413 --> 00:08:02,940
Okay, so I'm not a warrior.

121
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:06,460
I'm just really cute with
a great figure. Say what?

122
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:07,820
But even so,

123
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:13,086
I at least want to be strong
enough not to endanger the others.

124
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:16,420
Especially this time, for Vivi.

125
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:19,650
Hmm?

126
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:40,360
Usopp, I know you understand how I feel.

127
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,700
We're not like the others.

128
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,500
They're all as strong as monsters.

129
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:51,937
In a fight, they can rely on their
own power to defeat almost any enemy.

130
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:56,680
But us, we're just a couple of ordinary
humans with no special abilities.

131
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:00,640
When a battle starts, you
and I are just in the way.

132
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:03,566
We're a burden to the others.

133
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:05,582
We can't even protect ourselves.

134
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:10,797
If we're going to fight
beside them, we need weapons.

135
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:13,360
Really powerful ones. Or else...

136
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:23,217
Isn't that the reason you're
always inventing new weapons?

137
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,637
So you'll be able to hold your own
in a battle with them without shame?

138
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,550
Am I right?

139
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,020
It's the same for me.

140
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:33,500
To help Vivi.

141
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:36,137
I want to fight with my own two hands.

142
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,720
Will you help me or not?

143
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:42,159
We don't have much time
left till we reach Alabasta.

144
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,330
You're right.

145
00:09:48,413 --> 00:09:50,877
I guess you can't turn me
into a warrior overnight.

146
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,842
Sorry for being so unreasonable.

147
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,768
Unreasonable maybe, but
it's not impossible.

148
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:03,619
Hey, were you suggesting there's
something the mighty Usopp can't do?

149
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,170
Yeah?

150
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,117
Does that mean you're
really going to do it?

151
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,030
I love you!

152
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,240
Thank you, Usopp!

153
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:13,117
Now, as to the matter of the
cost, this won't be cheap!

154
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,357
I really, really mean it!

155
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,270
Thank you!

156
00:10:15,353 --> 00:10:16,837
Yeah, we covered the gratitude part.

157
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:18,637
But top-of-the-line weapons aren't free!

158
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,757
I'm counting on you, Kay!

159
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:20,840
Hold on a minute!

160
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,660
Relax, boys.

161
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,136
You're off the hook.

162
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,757
What am

163
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:33,840
I

164
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,750
doing?

165
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:42,640
I'm jumping at noises now.

166
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:50,600
And after I shot my mouth off in front
of Usopp like that, I'm ready, aren't I?

167
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,260
To fight for VD?

168
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,840
After all, Usopp kept his promise.

169
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,037
Okay, I'll fight!

170
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:10,120
If it's just that one
woman I should be able to?

171
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,280
Give it up, girl.

172
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:37,700
It's useless.

173
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:39,900
Miss Doublefinger.

174
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:43,080
But what was that
spear-like weapon she used?

175
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,535
Does she have Devil Fruit powers, too?

176
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,487
I know what you're thinking.

177
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:51,650
You're right.

178
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:53,207
I ate the Spike Spike Fruit.

179
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:57,297
It granted me the power to release
spikes from anywhere on my body.

180
00:11:57,380 --> 00:12:00,337
Spikes that can pierce right
through a solid stone wall.

181
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:03,317
If I slip up just once, she'll
make a pincushion out of me,

182
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,037
and that'll be the end of the story.

183
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:05,950
What?

184
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:09,214
Don't tell me you're actually
going to try and fight me.

185
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,310
Yes?

186
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:15,400
It can call upon clouds.

187
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:17,540
It can summon forth the rain.

188
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,020
It can create the wind itself.

189
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,857
My marvelous invention can cause disaster.

190
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,520
with its elemental power!

191
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:30,500
Stay away, or feel the
force of my climb-a-tact!

192
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:31,850
Climb-a?

193
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:32,840
What now?

194
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:36,160
For sunny weather, find take the world!

195
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,340
Wow, look at that!

196
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:42,000
It made dubs appear!

197
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,640
Dump thing!

198
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,000
Are you alright?

199
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,560
Okay, that was just the first try.

200
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,237
Besides, now we've gotten
her to lower her guard.

201
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,800
Very clever, Usopp.

202
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,252
This time you've hacked!

203
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,760
Cloudy Timbal!

204
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,035
And now we've got some pretty flowers!

205
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,740
Piece of junk!

206
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,430
Hmm.

207
00:13:14,513 --> 00:13:17,960
I don't know her story,
but what a poor kid.

208
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,040
Try again!

209
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,399
Save the princess!

210
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,170
Cannons!

211
00:13:25,253 --> 00:13:26,140
Bring cannons in!

212
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,980
Destroy the gates! Bury!

213
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:34,300
D .A .C. says flute!

214
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:43,400
What the?

215
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:14,225
Maybe now we can have a
little peace and quiet.

216
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,200
What a stubborn girl.

217
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:51,137
You're just wasting your time
dodging my attacks, you know?

218
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,337
You haven't got a chance.

219
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:53,657
I do too.

220
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:58,397
These instructions say there
are tons more attacks now.

221
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:03,577
Be a good girl and stay
right where you are.

222
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:07,497
That way I'll be able to kill you
without causing you too much pain.

223
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:09,617
Oh?

224
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,777
Does this.

225
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:12,978
This show of yours has a second act.

226
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:15,860
Forecast thunder!

227
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:17,740
Thunder Tempo!

228
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:27,860
Thunder Tempo.

229
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:30,920
Thunder Tempo. Thunder... Finger!

230
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:32,620
Stinger!

231
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,240
My cheek is bleeding.

232
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:55,980
Am I going to die like this?

233
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,220
I am, Marta.

234
00:15:58,640 --> 00:15:59,980
I'm going to die.

235
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,540
And I'll haunt him!

236
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,940
Long-nosed fool!

237
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,480
Long-nosed fool!

238
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:07,137
Long-nosed...

239
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:09,161
Why didn't he make a real weapon?

240
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:11,690
What's this?

241
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:15,660
So, I'll kill you now. Okay?

242
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:26,000
How is she doing that?

243
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:27,260
And why?

244
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:32,920
Hedgehog! Stay there!

245
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,140
Too close!

246
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:39,260
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait! Hold on!

247
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:40,960
Listen, hold on!

248
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:41,950
Just a minute!

249
00:16:42,033 --> 00:16:42,863
Can't you give a girl a minute?

250
00:16:42,946 --> 00:16:43,979
I'm not ready yet!

251
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:44,910
Come on!

252
00:16:44,993 --> 00:16:45,823
Ceasefire!

253
00:16:45,906 --> 00:16:46,736
No fair timeouts! Stop!

254
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,474
I can't stay out in the open like this!

255
00:16:58,220 --> 00:16:59,120
This is it!

256
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,460
Time for you to get skewered!

257
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:03,840
No! Thank you!

258
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:24,777
Well, it looks like she's got a little
more battle experience than I thought.

259
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:27,320
Not that it'll help. Where was it?

260
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:30,380
I saw it.

261
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:32,137
There was something that looked useful

262
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:34,985
somewhere in these
climate-hacked instructions.

263
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,682
Damn it, where?

264
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:37,910
That's it.

265
00:17:37,993 --> 00:17:39,997
Next time you're at a
party and things are slow,

266
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:43,477
just use these little tricks I've written
up, and things will really start to jump.

267
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:44,854
People will love them!

268
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:50,220
I'll kill you!

269
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:55,097
Oh, by the way, I've jotted down a
few battle configurations on the back.

270
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,140
On the back?

271
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:04,810
Let's see.

272
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:07,667
Where could you be hiding
yourself this time?

273
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:08,650
Little kitty

274
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,657
I'm through running and hiding.

275
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:22,137
I may not look it, but during
my eight years as a thief,

276
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:25,820
I survived all kinds of
crises, all by myself.

277
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:31,297
You can't treat me like
some ordinary girl now!

278
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:32,540
Bring it on, hussy!

279
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:36,040
Kitty found her claws.

280
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,820
Well then, show me what you've got.

281
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:40,220
You've got it!

282
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:41,720
Taste my real power!

283
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:45,220
The battle configurations of the Climatat.

284
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:48,696
First, understand the
characteristics of each section.

285
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:52,780
Each one can shoot off air bubbles,
either by shaking or blowing.

286
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:55,400
The first shoots hot air.

287
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,600
Heat ball!

288
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,840
What's this? It's warm.

289
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:04,720
Next shoots cool air.

290
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:07,980
Cool ball!

291
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,200
Ah, how pleasant.

292
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:12,627
The last shoots electricity!

293
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,300
Thunder ball!

294
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:18,840
Oh my, that tingled.

295
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,397
Of course these techniques
aren't quite finished yet?

296
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:24,097
So if you use them at parties,
you need to be careful.

297
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:25,651
Then why write them down?

298
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,520
Look, are we done here?

299
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:34,860
Sewing Stinger!

300
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,410
Please, please!

301
00:19:36,493 --> 00:19:38,397
Something I can use for
battle, not for party!

302
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:41,304
Some real technique,
something I can fight with!

303
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:46,800
I'm sorry, girl.

304
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,699
But I've had enough of these games.

305
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,260
Stinger, step!

306
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:07,960
I see.

307
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:10,397
The heat ball and cool ball join together.

308
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:14,637
When they stop spinning, the bubbles
hit each other, creating an airflow,

309
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,520
generating a powerful wind.

310
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,220
Brilliant, Usopp.

311
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,997
The cyclone tempo is like
an ordinary boomerang,

312
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:24,237
so if you take it outside after the party
to play with, you have to watch out.

313
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,960
He really doesn't get it.

314
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,980
But let's see here. Maybe I...

315
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,180
What kind of weapon is that?

316
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,518
Don't you dare turn your back on me!

317
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:43,817
To turn your back to your enemy
in the middle of a battle.

318
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,135
You didn't value your life too highly.

319
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,925
I changed the air density
by using a cool ball.

320
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:07,077
The temperature difference caused
a refraction of light known as...

321
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,320
A mirage.

322
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,500
No way.

323
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:11,020
At this distance?

324
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,920
We can't win with power.

325
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:21,020
If we're gonna survive,
we gotta use our brains.

326
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,820
That's how we fight, right?

327
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:27,500
Used properly, this can make miracles.

328
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:30,651
I'd say this is the perfect weapon for me.

329
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:36,740
Okay, Spiky, I'm ready.

330
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:39,240
Now why don't you give up?

331
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:47,840
Well, well, you're alive.

332
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,340
Oh, man! Sanji!

333
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:51,810
You're hurt.

334
00:21:54,380 --> 00:21:56,637
So, does this mean that you beat up Mr.

335
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:57,550
Two?

336
00:21:57,633 --> 00:21:58,463
Better believe it.

337
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,070
Here.

338
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:01,950
My goggles!

339
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,557
So you got them back for
me from that creep, huh?

340
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,470
Thank you, Sanji.

341
00:22:05,553 --> 00:22:06,656
Oh, you're the best.

342
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,090
Wait a minute.

343
00:22:08,173 --> 00:22:09,003
They're broken!

344
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:11,297
In that case, I take
back everything I said!

345
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:12,617
Thanks for nothing, you jerk!

346
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,337
And they were the latest bottles, too!

347
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:16,957
Do you have any idea what I
had to do to get these things?

348
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,037
Hey, look at that.

349
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,460
Look at my poor goggles! Whoa.

350
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:24,319
That must be the auxiliary
force for the rebel army.

351
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:26,255
There's more of them?

352
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:27,660
Looks like it.

353
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:31,274
I guess Phoebe wasn't able
to stop the fighting in time.

354
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,340
This is just great.

355
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:35,440
What the hell?

356
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:38,777
Hey, Eyelash, it's about
time you showed up.

357
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:39,937
Where have you been hiding?

358
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:41,277
Let's hurry to the palace.

359
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,557
Maybe there's still a way
we can help Phoebe out.

360
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:44,740
Come on. Wait.

361
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:46,222
Usopp, move it.

362
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,793
I'm coming, I'm coming.

363
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:50,560
Hey, Eyelash, give me a lift. Wait, stop.

364
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:51,737
Don't you see the bandages?

365
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:53,585
Help a ninja man out, will ya?

366
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:56,480
No, father!

367
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:03,260
Let the king go, crocodile. At once!

368
00:23:05,580 --> 00:23:07,600
Phoebe, I'm sorry.

369
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,280
I failed you.

370
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:10,420
And the nation.

371
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:15,720
I didn't use the chance you
risked your life for. Oh, father.

372
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:25,057
Let me tell you a little something.

373
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:28,434
I have no intention of keeping
you or your father alive.

374
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,200
When a kingdom dies out,

375
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:33,967
it only seems natural its royal
family should die out as well.

376
00:23:35,140 --> 00:23:37,980
But first, before I take the throne,

377
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:43,106
there's something I need to ask the current
king, if you have a moment, that is.

378
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:49,480
In fact, this has been my
goal from the very beginning.

379
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:55,400
Cobra, tell me, where's the Pluton?

380
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:09,060
Oh, Ken, you know that name.
